# Per-parameter descriptor, the Cyphal projection of the I2C parameter
# window. The host queries index
# 0..num_params-1 — index 0's response also carries num_params — to learn each
# declared parameter's name, unit, allowed values, default, and current value.
# `register.Access` carries the value alone; this service carries the full
# descriptor a value can't. An out-of-range index returns num_params with an
# empty name.

uint8 index

@extent 48 * 8

---

uint8 num_params        # total parameters the loaded driver declares
uint8 param_type        # 0=enum, 1=range (ranges are future work)
uint32 default_value    # value the driver shipped with
uint32 current_value    # value currently applied on-device
uint32[<=16] values     # allowed values (enum list); array length is the count
uint8[<=8] unit         # physical unit (ASCII)
uint8[<=16] name        # parameter name (ASCII)

@extent 256 * 8
